<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech PM Klaus says no talks with c.bank on rates.</title>
<headline>Czech PM Klaus says no talks with c.bank on rates.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said on Wednesday he had not held talks with the central bank on changing interest rates, and that easing monetary policy was up to the central bank itself.</p>
<p>But he added at a news conference outlining a series of measures to help jump start the economy including heavy budget cuts, that &quot;there must be an inverse development of monetary and fiscal policy&quot;.</p>
</text>
